& [Term_MetadataClaim] means caller-decodable declaration without carrier ownership
  + contains bounded logical identity complete scope completion disposition roles and causal relation
  + strict DeserializeOwned permits transport validation only
  - not: a digest carrier binding observation admission issuance occurrence or physical fact

& [Term_Carrier] means a complete current output-only supplied ancestry value
  + arrives as an owned typed function argument
  + retains private construction current profile assembly and transitive ancestors
  + remains Serialize only
  - not: metadata bytes digest text locator summary or proof of world origin

& [Term_Binding] means a successful pure association between one metadata role and one complete carrier
  + constructed only after exact role and carrier-exposed joins validate
  + retains both values and derives Serialize only
  - not: caller transport production admission or a physical acquisition lineage

& [Term_Invocation] means the one pure three-argument construction boundary
  + consumes one strict metadata plan first carrier and second carrier
  + validates rederives reconciles and atomically releases one result or one fault
  - not: a request that can encode carriers or any external-state operation

& [Term_RoundTrip] means same-type strict serde only for metadata
  + every field and closed variant survives canonical serialize/decode equality
  + unknown omitted aliased defaulted flattened or compatibility data refuses
  - not: reconstructing a carrier binding or result from serialized output

& [Term_OutputOnly] means absence of DeserializeOwned and alternate production construction
  + applies transitively to any value owning a current carrier or current reconciliation output
  + remains testable at compile time and inspectable through serialization and immutable getters
  - not: secret authentic admitted issued trusted or physically proven

& [Term_CarrierDerived] means exposed by the current complete carrier graph and checked exactly
  + encoding profile limits root relative path root kind root volume serial root file ID assembly profile digest profile and reconciliation profile
  + value still remains supplied semantic data
  - not: a claim that Windows or a producer observed it

& [Term_MetadataOnly] means structurally declared and compared between roles
  + candidate root reference volume-GUID path scanner/forms/receipt relation policy predecessor admission and predecessor receipt coordinates
  + never labeled carrier-derived or physically established
  - not: optional weak or ignorable

& [Term_CompleteScope] means the union of carrier-exposed and metadata-only coordinates
  + every coordinate remains mandatory
  + equality between roles is structural over the whole product
  + carrier-exposed coordinates additionally join to each owned carrier
  - not: duplicate sources of authority or a partial comparison view

& [Term_RoleBinding] means fixed First and Second association
  + first metadata binds only the first carrier argument and second metadata only the second
  + causal endpoints bind exact metadata identities independently of reconciliation left/right labels
  - not: physical time or operand order

& [Term_TraitFeasible] means the complete planned Rust derive graph compiles under existing dependencies
  + metadata types implement Serialize plus DeserializeOwned
  + current and new carrier-bearing types fail DeserializeOwned assertions
  + no predecessor type or dependency must change
  - not: a prose belief or runtime surrogate

& [Term_HistoricalInvalidation] means the old signature cannot authorize code
  + original source SJS canonical lock proof review signature and invalidation remain immutable evidence
  + 0.2 receives new UUIDs hashes and gates
  - not: deleting history or silently mutating the old canonical path

& [InheritedNonclaims] remain exact
  + no uniqueness collision freedom event occurrence time proof producer identity causal witness physical origin quiescence atomicity snapshot freshness present truth admission issuance receipt conversion consumption effect persistence remote FPGA Minecraft or neural authority
  + CompleteClaimed Equal NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual and ClaimOnly retain their narrow meanings

& [LanguageClosure] passes
  + overloaded transport and ownership terms are separated
  + every carrier join is classified
  + historical generation meaning is explicit
  + source revision required is false
  + implementation authority is absent
  + execution authority is absent
  + physical authority is absent
  + next is independent corrective constraint extraction and reapplication
